  "summary": "The code suffered from critical security flaws regarding open redirects and inefficient regex handling. I have refactored the validation logic to use a pre-compiled, anchored regex that enforces the 'https' protocol, and updated the function signature to follow PEP 8 standards.",
  "fixed_code": "from flask import Flask, redirect, request\nimport re\nfrom typing import Union\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n# Pre-compile regex at module level for performance and security\n# Anchored to start of string and enforces https protocol\nALLOWED_TARGET_PATTERN = re.compile(r'^https://(www|beta)\\.example\\.com/')\n\n@app.route('/redirect')\ndef redirect_to_target() -> str:\n    '''\n    Get target URL from request, validate against allowed domain pattern,\n    then redirect to the target URL.\n    '''\n    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n    if target and ALLOWED_TARGET_PATTERN.match(target):\n        return redirect(target)\n    else:\n        return \"Invalid target\""
